sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R2-R4 and 5 (one swamp-role SSH identity); Orbit only adds its own keys and never rewrites authorized_keys (Nov 1 incident); flow-tighten rule 22.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: node:ssh-access:converge
  %% kind: node.ssh_access_converge
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: node:ssh-access:converge<br/>12 · Node id
  %%> Command:
  %%> - MCP tool `node-ssh-access-converge` with node `12`; API `POST /nodes/12/ssh-access/converge`
  %%> - syntax: `<node>`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Node only; the keys come from Orbit's records, never from the request
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - makes Node 12's managed account accept the Swamp Node's SSH identity and the operator keys recorded in Orbit
  %%> - keeps every other key in `authorized_keys` exactly as it is
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the MCP tool and the API; the `orbit` CLI has no command for it yet
  Note over GW: Validate, list the keys<br/>task #5133 · Node 12
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - Node 12 is an active, managed Linux Node with stored SSH host keys
  %%> - its managed account is not `root`
  %%> - no other SSH access change runs for Node 12; the Gateway holds one lock per Node
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - Orbit's keys: the `swamp` role's public key from Node 209, then each operator key recorded in Orbit, in a stable order
  %%> - their digest
  %%> Reuse:
  %%> - a succeeded or running task with the same digest for Node 12 is returned instead of a new one
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5133 recorded with the full intent; no private key in it
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-ssh-access
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - Orbit's keys and their digest, and the managed account
  %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5133
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Write the Orbit keys<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/authorized_key
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - adds each of Orbit's keys to the managed account's `authorized_keys` when it is missing, one behavior per key
  %%> Never:
  %%> - removes, reorders or changes another line, so operator keys Orbit does not manage keep their access
  %%> How:
  %%> - the official `@swamp/cfgmgmt/authorized_key` behavior over SSH from 209, as the managed account
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - a Node that does not accept the `swamp` role identity yet; Node bootstrap adds that first key
  SW->>N: Log in with Swamp identity<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · true
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - opens a new SSH session with the `swamp` role identity only, and runs `true`
  %%> Returns:
  %%> - the end check; the Gateway reads it from Swamp's run data
  %%> Why:
  %%> - access only counts as ready when the Swamp identity really logs in
  alt login works
    N-->>SW: exit 0
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - every check passed
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the keys' digest<br/>access ready · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Node 12's SSH access digest is the digest of Orbit's keys
    %%> - task #5133 succeeds
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: write refused or denied
    %%> When:
    %%> - a key cannot be added, or the Swamp identity is refused
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Keep the old digest<br/>task failed · rerun is safe
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Node 12's recorded SSH access stays as it was
    %%> - task #5133 fails
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - added keys stay; there is no rollback
    %%> - other keys are never touched, so operator access stays
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again after fixing the cause; keys already there are left as they are
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5133
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
